<section aria-labelledby="reference-usage">
  <h2 id="reference-usage">Using this reference</h2>
  <p>Choose a <strong>Language</strong> and, where available, a <strong>Client</strong> variant for the examples. <strong>Examples</strong> switches between <strong>Simple</strong> and <strong>With error handling</strong>. Your choices apply to every example and stay selected as you browse.</p>
  <p>Start with <a href="#initialization">Initialization</a> below and <a href="<%= escape_html(documentation_url(page: 'authentication')) %>">Authentication</a> for credentials. Open <a href="<%= escape_html(documentation_url(page: 'resources')) %>">Resources</a> to browse the API, then choose a resource to see its actions, parameters and examples. The sidebar follows the action in view; breadcrumbs link to parent resources.</p>
  <p>Search finds resources, actions and input or output parameters. Follow a result to its reference entry.</p>
  <p>While signed out, the reference shows all declared resources, actions and parameters. Sign in to show only those available to your account. Each API request still checks permissions for the requested operation.</p>
</section>
